menu "ADC signal source (Lab 4)"

    config LAB_SIM_ADC
        bool "Use simulated ADC (adc_sim) instead of the real adc_oneshot driver"
        default y
        help
            When enabled (the default -- required for QEMU, which has no
            analog signal to sample), this component compiles a synthetic
            lab_adc_init()/lab_adc_read_raw() pair: a nominal 1.5 V input
            mapped through a fixed 12-bit ADC transfer function that
            deliberately carries a gain error (x1.03), an offset error
            (+25 LSB) and Gaussian noise (sigma ~= 8 LSB, from a seeded PRNG
            so the sequence is identical from one boot to the next) --
            see adc_sim/README.md for the exact ground-truth numbers.
            main/lab_adc_oneshot.c (the real driver, hardware only) is
            compiled OUT in this case.

            When disabled, this component's source file is empty (see its
            "#if CONFIG_LAB_SIM_ADC" guard) and main/lab_adc_oneshot.c's real
            adc_oneshot driver provides lab_adc_init()/lab_adc_read_raw()
            instead, sampling ADC1 channel 0 (GPIO0) for real.

            Same lab_adc.h API either way -- app_main() does not change.

endmenu
